        "text": "**Constructing Project Architecture**\n\nI'm currently architecting the multi-file Python project. I need to generate nine new Python files while keeping `upsert_document.py` as is. I'm focusing on integrating each \"scored\" file with a concrete external NoSQL database; `SAME-SCENARIO` and `LATER-STEP` in particular.\n\n\n**Defining Database Integration**\n\nNow I'm diving deeper into the database aspect. I'm leaning toward AWS DynamoDB, considering its managed nature and compatibility. I'll utilize `boto3` to interact with the database. I'm focusing on creating `database_models.py` to define the data structures and also `database_client.py` to handle the connection and common database operations. The core of this work will be establishing how the external database interacts with the rest of the project.\n\n\n**Planning File Creation**\n\nI've examined the structure of `upsert_document.py` to understand its interaction with a NoSQL store. Based on that and the project's requirements, I'm opting for AWS DynamoDB. I'll utilize `boto3` to handle the AWS integration. I've broken down the helper file creation, now into models and database clients. Next will be implementations.\n\n\n",
